# 19. DEFINITION OF DONE

The game is not considered complete merely because a 3D character can run.

The release must include:

- A complete main menu.
- Playable third-person movement.
- Responsive desktop and mobile controls.
- All three gameplay phases.
- Theft success and failure outcomes.
- Vehicle progression.
- Balloon escape and helicopter pursuit.
- Police escalation.
- Functional gadgets and cooldowns.
- Coin collection and score calculation.
- Procedural city segments.
- Object pooling and cleanup.
- Game-over and restart.
- Upgrade shop and persistent local progression.
- Sound effects and feedback.
- Tutorial and settings.
- Responsive HUD.
- Error handling and performance safeguards.
- A production build that can be deployed to a static web host.

No major button should be decorative or nonfunctional. No gameplay feature should be represented by a placeholder when it is claimed to be implemented.

